Both, split pretty cleanly:

**Employee/Business Side (configuration — set up once)**
- `minDays` — business rule (e.g., "we need at least 2 days notice")
- `maxDays` — business rule (e.g., "can't book more than 10 days out")
- `cutOffTime` — business rule (e.g., "requests after 2 PM roll to next day")
- `exclusions` — business rule (e.g., "we don't work weekends")

These define *how the business operates* and would typically be hardcoded or pulled from a config/database, not entered per request.

**Customer Side (runtime input — changes every call)**
- `requestDateTime` — the timestamp of when the customer is submitting the request

That's the only dynamic input. The customer doesn't control any of the rules — the code just uses their submission time to calculate what window is available to them *given* the business's constraints.

